module latte
kind library

# Latte is pure Beans. There is no vendored C, no `csrc` row and no `link`
# row, and that is a property worth keeping: the core (frames, builder,
# serializer, differ) imports no I/O at all, which is what leaves a
# WebAssembly render mode possible later. `test.sh` builds the core for
# wasm32-unknown-unknown to hold that line — a core that grows an import of
# std.fs or std.net fails that leg, not a code review.
#
# latte.bx, the markup compiler under bx/, is build-time only. It imports
# std.fs. Nothing under the module root imports latte.bx, so a program that
# ships a latte page never links a compiler.

# `latte.web` — the circuit endpoint — is the one package under this module
# that imports espresso. Nothing at the module root imports `latte.web`, so a
# static-page program never loads espresso and the wasm leg is unaffected.
require github.com/beans-lang/espresso v0.3.0
